file_manager: unpack sliced .3mf uploads to G-code

OrcaSlicer's "Use 3MF instead of G-code" (and Bambu-style plate files)
uploads a .gcode.3mf. Moonraker stored it as a plain file and answered
201, so the printer never printed it (issue #35). A sliced .3mf is now
unpacked on upload: Metadata/plate_<N>.gcode becomes <name>.gcode (several
plates: <name>_plate<N>.gcode, none started), the .3mf is dropped, and the
upload goes on as that G-code (metadata, print=true). A .3mf with no
sliced plate, a broken zip or an implausible size is refused with 400
and a message. An optional "plate" form field picks the plate of a .3mf
with several. kiln_3mf.py has only the standard library, so
tools/test_moonraker_3mf.py tests it on the laptop.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)

